      "note": [
        "As of the fourth quarter 2021, this table replaces the previous table for seasonally adjusted current account and capital account. The table is, unlike the previous, aggregation consistent and contains account items divided between export and import.\r\n Aggregation consistency means that sub-items add up to the total item. For example, the sum of seasonally adjusted goods and seasonally adjusted services is equal to seasonally adjusted item Trade in goods and services. Account items for exports and imports are also consistent with the total balance.",
        "The publication of the third quarter of 2022 includes revised data on compensation of employees to and from abroad from 2015 and onwards. The reason for this revision is that the Balance of Payments has introduced new sources. Data on compensation of employees to Sweden is compiled using the Swedish income and tax register (IoT). Data on compensation of employees from Sweden is compiled using declarations of employer on individual level (AGI). "
      ],
